Direct3D 10: indexable temporaries declared as arrays

A Direct3D 10 shader's indexable temporaries (x0[6] and the like) were declared one register
at a time and then indexed with a computed offset. A renderer that interprets the shader does
not mind. virgl's host turns it into GLSL, where the registers are separate variables: the
shader did not compile, the host counted that as an error of the context and drew nothing
more for it (Windows' second geometry assessment, which then "ran" at 12 000 frames a second).
They are now declared as one array each, which the host translates to a GLSL array.

diff -ru a/src/gallium/frontends/d3d10umd/ShaderTGSI.c b/src/gallium/frontends/d3d10umd/ShaderTGSI.c
--- a/src/gallium/frontends/d3d10umd/ShaderTGSI.c
+++ b/src/gallium/frontends/d3d10umd/ShaderTGSI.c
@@ -2129,7 +2129,9 @@
          {
             uint i;
 
-            /* XXX: Add true indexable temps to gallium.
+            /* One array of temporaries, declared as an array: a renderer that turns the
+             * shader into source text (virgl's host) can only index what it knows to be
+             * one.
              */
 
             assert(opcode.specific.dcl_indexable_temp.index <
@@ -2140,8 +2142,14 @@
             sx.indexable_temp_offsets[opcode.specific.dcl_indexable_temp.index] =
                sx.declared_temps;
 
-            for (i = 0; i < opcode.specific.dcl_indexable_temp.count; i++) {
-               sx.temps[sx.declared_temps + i] = ureg_DECL_temporary(ureg);
+            if (opcode.specific.dcl_indexable_temp.count) {
+               struct ureg_dst array =
+                  ureg_DECL_array_temporary(ureg, opcode.specific.dcl_indexable_temp.count, false);
+
+               for (i = 0; i < opcode.specific.dcl_indexable_temp.count; i++) {
+                  sx.temps[sx.declared_temps + i] = array;
+                  sx.temps[sx.declared_temps + i].Index += i;
+               }
             }
             sx.declared_temps += opcode.specific.dcl_indexable_temp.count;
          }
